<p id="mw2w">The strong equivalence<sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mw3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3g">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3w">]</span></span></a></sup> says that two systems <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt98" id="mw4A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"S_1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle S_{1}}">
  <semantics>
