        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle ({\textit {val}}(b),val(a))\not \in {\textit {valprefs}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/95fe8ddcd51d86ffe8269ad361dfe0d28e264523" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; margin-right: -0.021ex; width:25.212ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle ({\textit {val}}(b),val(a))\not \in {\textit {valprefs}}}"/></span>, that is the value advanced by <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt144" id="mwATE" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"b"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle b}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>b</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle b}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f11423fbb2e967f986e36804a8ae4271734917c3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:0.998ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle b}"/></span> is not preferred to the one advanced by <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt145" id="mwATI" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"a"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle a}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>a</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle a}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ffd2487510aa438433a2579450ab2b3d557e5edc" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.23ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle a}"/></span>.</li></ul>
<p id="mwATM">One remarks that an attack succeeds if both arguments are associated to the same value, or if there is no preference between their respective values.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwATQ" aria-labelledby="Assumption-based_argumentation_frameworks"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Assumption-based_argumentation_frameworks">Assumption-based argumentation frameworks</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Argumentation_framework&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Assumption-based argumentation frameworks"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwATU">In assumption-based argumentation (ABA) frameworks, arguments are defined as a set of rules and attacks are defined in terms of assumptions and contraries.</p>

<p id="mwATY">Formally, an assumption-based argumentation framework is a tuple <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt146" id="mwATc" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\langle \\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{R}, \\mathcal{A}, \\overline{\\textvisiblespace} \\rangle"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \langle {\mathcal {L}},{\mathcal {R}},{\mathcal {A}},{\overline {\mathrm {\textvisiblespace} }}\rangle }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo fence="false" stretchy="false">⟨<!-- ⟨ --></mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">L</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">R</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">A</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mover>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mo>␣</mo>
              </mrow>
            </mrow>
            <mo accent="false">¯<!-- ¯ --></mo>
          </mover>
        </mrow>
        <mo fence="false" stretchy="false">⟩<!-- ⟩ --></mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \langle {\mathcal {L}},{\mathcal {R}},{\mathcal {A}},{\overline {\mathrm {\textvisiblespace} }}\rangle }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/06b43f349d3697398b53c4cf0f1526ce07101a7c" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.171ex; width:11.921ex; height:4.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \langle {\mathcal {L}},{\mathcal {R}},{\mathcal {A}},{\overline {\mbox{\textvisiblespace} }}\rangle }"/></span>,<sup about="#mwt150" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-10" id="mwATg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt153" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwATw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAT0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT4">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt156" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-12" id="mwAUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUI">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUM">]</span></span></a></sup> where</p>
<ul id="mwAUQ"><li id="mwAUU"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt157" id="mwAUY" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\langle \\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{R} \\rangle"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \langle {\mathcal {L}},{\mathcal {R}}\rangle }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
