<p id="mwAVY">As a consequence of defining an ABA, an argument can be represented in a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_(data_structure)" title="Tree (data structure)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAVc">tree-form</a>.<sup about="#mwt170" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_10-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-10" id="mwAVg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVo">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVs">]</span></span></a></sup> Formally, given a deductive system <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt171" id="mwAVw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\langle \\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{R} \\rangle"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \langle {\mathcal {L}},{\mathcal {R}}\rangle }">
  <semantics>
